C++20 std::erase_if on std::vector<int>.

Reclassified CORE -> KNOWNBUG by the member-typedef conformance fix
([temp.inst]/1-2, [dcl.typedef]).  Previously this passed only because the
non-conformant *truncated* std::vector had its operations havoc'd -- demonstrably
unsound: with the truncated container even `__CPROVER_assert(v.size() == 999)`
reports VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL, because symex executes 0 instructions of the
real container.  The fix makes the front end conformant and symex now executes
the REAL std::vector / erase_if machinery (exactly what g++ -O0 emits), which
does not complete within resources.

Second-tier verification-PERFORMANCE item, not a conformance one; the previous
"pass" was unsound.  Reclassify back to CORE once symex is tractable on the real
container.
See doc/architectural/cpp-class-template-instantiation-plan.md.
